    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="1005" n="881" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg881"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11 G 93/1157</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hartman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic">January 4,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 1.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 632</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise the Department
                    that in a conversation with President Tamayo yesterday afternoon, in answer to
                    my inquiry, he assured me that the daily deposits on account of the service <pb
                        facs="1006" n="882" xml:id="pg882"/> of the Guayaquil and Quito Railway
                    bonds would be continued, notwithstanding the fact that the decree of March 8,
                        1920,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d810-f1"/> ordering the deposits had expired on
                    December 31, 1920. He stated that in his opinion the decree was unnecessary as
                    the obligation on the Government of Ecuador to make the deposits was contained
                    in the contracts.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d810-f2"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. S. Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d810-f1" n="10" xml:id="d810-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; purport given in telegram no. 14, Mar. 18, 1920, from the Minister
                    in Ecuador, <ref target="frus1920v02#pg_195"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1920, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p.
                        195</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d810-f2" n="11" xml:id="d810-f2-content">
                <p>See despatch no. 525, Apr. 1, 1920, paragraph 6 as printed, from the Minister in
                    Ecuador, <ref target="frus1920v02#pg_198"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p.
                        198</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
